8. Additional Use Grant. (See below.)

Notwithstanding the non-production use restriction in Section 4(b) of the
Business Source License 1.1, Next Mavens grants You a limited Additional
Use Grant to use the Soostori SDK in Production Use, subject to the
limitations below.

8.1 Purpose-based and functional determination.

   Whether a particular Production Use is permitted or prohibited is
   determined by the PRODUCT'S (OR RELEVANT MODULE'S) PRIMARY PURPOSE
   AND SUBSTANTIAL FUNCTIONAL ROLE considered as a whole, and not by
   any individual feature, individual SDK capability, packaging model,
   distribution channel, or incidental similarity in capabilities.

   The determination is independent of:

     (a) the presence of any individual SDK capability (including but
         not limited to inventory, customers, sales, payments,
         products, business data, synchronization, authentication,
         reporting, invoicing, or multi-location management);
     (b) the industry, vertical, or customer segment the product
         serves;
     (c) the geographic market or deployment model;
     (d) the size of the customer or organization;
     (e) the product's name, marketing language, or pricing model;
     (f) the number of users, employees, seats, or installations;
     (g) whether the product is offered as open source or proprietary;
     (h) whether the product is sold as a standalone product, as a
         SaaS, as a white-label service, as part of a commercial
         software suite, as a separately marketed module, or
         embedded within a larger commercial platform.

   The terms "primary purpose," "substantial functional role,"
   "substantially equivalent," and "broad" necessarily involve judgment
   and legal interpretation.

   A non-competing application does NOT become prohibited merely
   because it contains an incidental POS-like, inventory, customer,
   payment, invoicing, reporting, or other business feature.

   FEATURE IS NOT THE SAME AS A COMPETING PRODUCT. PRIMARY PRODUCT
   PURPOSE AND SUBSTANTIAL FUNCTIONAL ROLE ARE THE DETERMINATION.

8.2 Permitted Production Use.

   You may use the Soostori SDK in Production Use in any software
   application, module, or service whose primary purpose and
   substantial functional role is NOT substantially equivalent to
   either:

     (a) a point-of-sale / checkout / sales-transaction-processing
         product offered as a commercial product (whether as a
         standalone product, SaaS, white-label service, suite
         component, or embedded module); or
     (b) an integrated general business-management platform whose
         primary purpose is broad day-to-day merchant or business
         operations management as a commercial product (whether as a
         standalone product, SaaS, white-label service, suite
         component, or embedded module).

   Permitted Production Use includes, without limitation, applications
   whose primary purpose is one or more of the following:

     (i)   accounting, bookkeeping, financial reporting, audit, or
           invoicing software;
     (ii)  logistics, supply chain, transportation, or fleet
           management;
     (iii) warehouse management, when its primary function is
           non-POS inventory operations;
     (iv)  e-commerce, online marketplace, or catalog publishing;
     (v)   customer relationship management (CRM), contact
           management, or marketing automation;
     (vi)  analytics, business intelligence, or reporting;
     (vii) field service or workforce operations;
     (viii) vertical-specific software for veterinary, medical,
           dental, salon, automotive, education, hospitality, or
           professional services, where the primary purpose is the
           vertical's domain rather than acting as a POS or general
           business-management platform;
     (ix)  restaurant, kitchen, reservation, ordering-assistance,
           or hospitality software where POS / general business
           management is NOT the primary purpose;
     (x)   internal business tools and dashboards;
     (xi)  developer tools, libraries, or frameworks that embed the
           Soostori SDK as an internal implementation detail where
           the primary purpose is NOT enabling competing POS or
           general business-management products;
     (xii) any other software whose primary purpose and substantial
           functional role is something other than acting as a POS
           or general business-management platform.

8.3 Prohibited Production Use.

   You may NOT use the Soostori SDK in Production Use to create,
   distribute, or operate a commercial product (whether as a
   standalone product, SaaS, white-label service, suite component,
   separately marketed module, or embedded within a larger commercial
   platform) whose primary purpose and substantial functional role
   is substantially equivalent to either:

     (a) a point-of-sale / checkout / sales-transaction-processing
         product offered as a commercial product; or
     (b) an integrated general business-management platform whose
         primary purpose is broad day-to-day merchant or business
         operations management as a commercial product.

   Without limiting the foregoing, the following are prohibited:

     (i)   creating, distributing, or operating a retail POS,
           supermarket POS, grocery POS, general merchant POS, multi-
           store POS platform, or merchant checkout platform whose
           primary purpose is to provide point-of-sale checkout and
           sales transaction processing;
     (ii)  creating, distributing, or operating a general small-and-
           medium-enterprise business-management platform whose
           primary purpose is broad day-to-day merchant or business
           operations management as an integrated commercial product;
     (iii) creating, distributing, or operating a white-label POS
           service or commercial SaaS whose primary product is
           providing POS or general business-management functionality
           to merchants;
     (iv)  creating, distributing, or operating a commercial POS or
           general business-management product regardless of customer
           segment, vertical, industry, geographic market, or
           deployment model;
     (v)   creating, distributing, or operating a commercial
           product whose primary product purpose is POS or general
           business-management functionality for merchants, even if
           packaged inside a larger commercial suite or hosted on
           a shared infrastructure;
     (vi)  creating, distributing, or operating a competing POS or
           general business-management product whose primary purpose
           is substantially equivalent to the Soostori product
           category.

8.4 Suite / module treatment.

   The prohibition in Section 8.3 applies whether the relevant product
   or module is:

     (a) sold as a standalone commercial product;
     (b) offered as a SaaS;
     (c) offered as a white-label service;
     (d) distributed as part of a commercial software suite;
     (e) provided as a separately marketed module; or
     (f) embedded into a larger commercial platform,

   IF the relevant product or module's primary purpose and substantial
   functional role is to provide the prohibited POS or general
   business-management functionality.

   Packaging does not create a loophole. A POS product packaged inside
   a larger commercial suite remains prohibited if its primary
   purpose is POS, and a non-competing product that contains an
   incidental POS-like feature remains permitted if its primary
   purpose is something other than POS.

   Examples:

     - A commercial ERP/business platform whose primary product
       purpose is broad merchant/business operations management
       remains prohibited even if it is technically marketed as part
       of a larger suite.
     - A commercial software suite whose relevant module is
       primarily a POS remains prohibited.
     - A CRM containing a small checkout/payment feature remains
       permitted if CRM is the primary purpose.
     - An e-commerce platform containing inventory functionality
       remains permitted if e-commerce is the primary purpose.
     - A restaurant management platform focused on reservations,
       kitchen coordination, or customer engagement remains permitted
       when POS is not the primary purpose.
     - A developer library that merely embeds Soostori internally
       remains permitted unless its primary purpose is enabling
       competing POS / general business-management products.

8.5 Vertical software rule.

   Industry does not determine the result. The same functional test
   applies regardless of industry or vertical.

   By way of example (and not of limitation):

     - Veterinary management software is permitted when its primary
       purpose is veterinary management; a veterinary POS whose
       primary purpose is POS is prohibited.
     - Restaurant reservation, kitchen, ordering-assistance, and
       customer-engagement software is permitted where POS / general
       business management is not the primary purpose; a restaurant
       POS whose primary purpose is POS is prohibited.
     - Salon appointment or operations software is permitted where
       POS is not the primary purpose; a salon POS whose primary
       purpose is POS is prohibited.
     - Medical clinic management is permitted where POS / general
       business management is not the primary purpose; a medical
       POS whose primary purpose is POS is prohibited.
     - Automotive shop management is permitted where POS / general
       business management is not the primary purpose; an
       automotive POS whose primary purpose is POS is prohibited.
     - Education software is permitted where POS / general business
       management is not the primary purpose; a school POS whose
       primary purpose is POS is prohibited.

8.6 Embedded SDK use.

   Ordinary embedded use of the Soostori SDK as a dependency in
   otherwise permitted commercial applications is permitted,
   including but not limited to:

     (a) internal libraries or frameworks that use the SDK as an
         internal implementation detail;
     (b) developer tools that embed the SDK as an implementation
         detail;
     (c) applications whose primary purpose is something other than
         acting as a POS or general business-management platform.

   Embedded use does not require a separate license, permission, or
   fee beyond what this Additional Use Grant provides.

8.7 SDK redistribution.

   You may NOT redistribute the Soostori SDK, modified or unmodified,
   as a competing SDK, developer platform, or developer toolkit
   whose primary purpose is enabling developers to create competing
   POS or general business-management products.

   This clause does NOT prohibit ordinary embedded dependency use of
   the SDK in otherwise permitted applications, nor does it prohibit
   internal libraries or frameworks that use the SDK where the
   primary purpose is NOT enabling competing POS or general business-
   management products.

   This clause does NOT prohibit ordinary applications merely because
   they depend on the SDK.

8.8 No additional restrictions.

   This Additional Use Grant does NOT impose any of the following:

     (a) user-count, employee-count, seat-count, or installation-
         count restrictions;
     (b) revenue, funding, or financial-size thresholds;
     (c) geographic restrictions;
     (d) industry-based or vertical-based exemptions or
         restrictions;
     (e) requirements to purchase or maintain a Soostori
         subscription for ordinary commercial use of the SDK;
     (f) restrictions on embedded use of the SDK as an internal
         dependency in otherwise permitted commercial applications;
     (g) restrictions on internal business tools or internal
         applications.

8.9 No subscription requirement.

   A developer or organization does NOT need to purchase or maintain
   a Soostori subscription merely because they use the Soostori SDK
   in an ordinary commercial application.

   Any requirement to obtain a Soostori subscription arises only from
   Soostori's separate terms of service for hosted or managed
   services, which is outside the scope of this License.

8.10 Prohibited examples (informational, not exhaustive):

     (a) retail POS, supermarket POS, grocery POS, general merchant
         POS, multi-store POS platform, or merchant checkout
         platform whose primary purpose is point-of-sale checkout and
         sales transaction processing;
     (b) general small-and-medium-enterprise business-management
         platform whose primary purpose is broad merchant/business
         operations management as an integrated commercial product;
     (c) white-label POS service or commercial SaaS whose primary
         product is POS or general business-management functionality
         for merchants;
     (d) commercial software suite whose relevant module is
         primarily a POS or general business-management product;
     (e) competing developer platform or SDK whose primary purpose is
         enabling third-party developers to build competing POS or
         general business-management products.

8.11 Permitted examples (informational, not exhaustive):

     (a) accounting, bookkeeping, financial reporting, audit, or
         invoicing software;
     (b) logistics, supply-chain, transportation, or fleet management
         software;
     (c) warehouse management software whose primary function is
         non-POS inventory operations;
     (d) e-commerce storefronts, online marketplaces, or catalog
         publishing platforms;
     (e) CRM, contact management, or marketing automation platforms;
     (f) analytics, business-intelligence, or reporting platforms;
     (g) field-service or workforce-operations applications;
     (h) veterinary, medical, dental, salon, automotive, education,
         hospitality, or professional-services vertical software
         whose primary purpose is the vertical's domain (not POS or
         general business management);
     (i) restaurant reservation, kitchen, ordering-assistance, or
         customer-engagement software (when POS is not the primary
         purpose);
     (j) internal business tools, dashboards, or reporting
         applications;
     (k) developer tools, libraries, or frameworks that embed the
         Soostori SDK as an internal implementation detail where
         the primary purpose is NOT enabling competing POS or general
         business-management products.

End of terms

